WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.820
SpaceX clarified that Ukraine seeks commercial starlink for offensive strikes while star-shield remains under U.S. government control. This is SpaceX Daily Episode 167. Texas tax structure, a Memphis revenue share, dragon splash down slip, then the engineering deep dive. Elon Musk in remarks and gadget carried from the New York Times Dealbook Summit said the drone campaign violates starlink's civilian service terms. He called Zellen Skies' version of star-shield speed

00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:33.500
limits false, and said Zelensky is not always truthful.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:39.160
Offensive operation calls, he said, sit with the U.S. Department of War, not with a private

00:00:39.160 --> 00:00:39.660
company.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:44.840
Starlink he added was never meant to help drone strikes that kill people, and any such

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:47.960
capability has to run through Starsheald as a separate system.

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:53.460
Zelensky had said speed caps on Starsheald terminals along the front and inside Russian

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:57.160
territory were hurting interceptor drones going after high-speed threats.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:03.240
Musk also pointed out that Ukraine had earlier rejected misuse claims, with officials arguing

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:07.240
the limits already in place would have made strikes into Russian territory physically

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:07.900
impossible.

00:01:08.812 --> 00:01:13.612
SpaceX said on X that a proposed Texas data center abatement would have given the county

00:01:13.612 --> 00:01:18.172
predictable revenue through payments in lieu of taxes, a fixed substitute for the

00:01:18.172 --> 00:01:21.532
usual property bill, while still backing further investment.

00:01:22.012 --> 00:01:26.532
Without the agreement, property owners now face greater year-to-year tax rate swings

00:01:26.532 --> 00:01:31.472
as computing equipment depreciates. Under the state's no-new revenue tax framework,

00:01:32.012 --> 00:01:37.252
rising property values generally drive tax rates down, but rapid depreciation of expensive

00:01:37.252 --> 00:01:42.792
hardware creates significant annual fluctuations. The abatement had been built to turn those swings

00:01:42.792 --> 00:01:47.212
into stable payments that would have given the county predictable income across the life of the

00:01:47.212 --> 00:01:52.352
project, and the company said it looks forward to further discussions with local jurisdictions on

00:01:52.352 --> 00:01:58.192
sustainable long-term revenue. Residents of one Memphis zip code, the commercial appeal reported,

00:01:58.772 --> 00:02:03.572
may receive a portion of tax revenue tied to a SpaceX AI project for home improvements.

00:02:04.152 --> 00:02:09.252
The outlet detailed the application process for eligible households seeking funds from the project's

00:02:09.252 --> 00:02:15.642
local economic contributions. Dragon's cargo capsule stood down from a November 19th California

00:02:15.642 --> 00:02:21.402
splashdown after SpaceX said teams continue monitoring weather, and the return now targets no

00:02:21.402 --> 00:02:26.822
earlier than November 20th. The spacecraft arrived at the station on October 15th carrying

00:02:26.822 --> 00:02:29.322
completed science experiments and lab hardware.

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:35.162
National aeronautics and space administration, or NASA, flight engineers have been packing

00:02:35.162 --> 00:02:41.262
3D bioprinted blood vessel samples, tissue printed layer by layer, along with antibiotic

00:02:41.262 --> 00:02:46.422
resistant bacteria specimens and protein crystal growth experiments for return analysis.

00:02:46.422 --> 00:02:46.542
Texas.

00:02:47.182 --> 00:02:52.102
Additional hardware includes a circadian lighting system, lights that follow the body's daily

00:02:52.102 --> 00:02:55.622
clock, and a space suit slated for refurbishment on the ground.

00:02:56.667 --> 00:03:03.007
Voyager 1, NASA Space Flight Reports, passed 26 billion kilometers from Earth at 516 in

00:03:03.007 --> 00:03:07.447
the morning eastern on November 18th, as far as light flies in a full day.

00:03:08.027 --> 00:03:12.687
The milestone came almost 50 years after it left Earth in September 1977.

00:03:12.687 --> 00:03:18.947
The probe followed the JST path aimed at Jupiter, Saturn, and Titan, after the original

00:03:18.947 --> 00:03:24.847
Grand Tour program was cut back for budget reasons in the early 1970s, then used gravitational

00:03:24.847 --> 00:03:30.567
assists, speed picked up by swinging past the outer planets to reach interstellar space.

00:03:31.475 --> 00:03:36.675
Planet Labs signed an agreement with Stokespace, the Motley Fool reported, to secure launch

00:03:36.675 --> 00:03:39.375
capacity of SpaceX retires the Falcon 9.

00:03:39.375 --> 00:03:44.735
The deal provides an alternative ride share option for the company's Earth observation satellites,

00:03:45.095 --> 00:03:50.775
and Planet Labs cited the need for diversified launch access as Falcon 9 flight rates remain high,

00:03:51.235 --> 00:03:57.175
and future retirement discussions continue in the industry. Gemini 4 Neon is now inside Cursor,

00:03:57.415 --> 00:04:03.395
the AI code editor, a post on X said, running at default effort and lifting a coding score called

00:04:03.395 --> 00:04:10.535
cursor bench 4.1 to 63.7% from 57.3% on the prior hydrogen version.

00:04:11.155 --> 00:04:16.195
Pricing is $3 per million input tokens and $15 per million output tokens.

00:04:16.835 --> 00:04:21.995
The model gives developers access to all agent tools including file search, web queries,

00:04:22.435 --> 00:04:27.135
terminal execution and browser control while remaining a third-party option build from

00:04:27.135 --> 00:04:29.135
prepaid credits on legacy plans.

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:36.514
Snap released EasyLens CLI, Cryptopolitan reported, a command line interface that lets developers

00:04:36.514 --> 00:04:42.094
describe an AR lens, an augmented reality camera effect, in plain language and lets

00:04:42.094 --> 00:04:46.634
Claude, Codex, and Cursor handle building, testing, and publishing.

00:04:47.174 --> 00:04:53.254
The tool works on Mac, Windows, and Linux and supports over 100 AR blocks, plus 50 AI

00:04:53.254 --> 00:04:54.294
asset generators.

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:59.674
A full lens game can move from initial idea to published experience in a single day without

00:04:59.674 --> 00:05:00.734
handwritten code.

00:05:01.154 --> 00:05:06.474
And developers enrolled in the Lens Plus Payouts program can earn revenue from CLI-built lenses

00:05:06.474 --> 00:05:11.174
after Snap distributed $1.8 million to community creators last month.

00:05:12.039 --> 00:05:17.839
On the hardware side, three years ago, Super Heavy Booster 9 and Ship 25 lifted off on

00:05:17.839 --> 00:05:23.599
Flight 2 with all 33 Raptors running through Ascent and Ship 25 lighting engines while

00:05:23.599 --> 00:05:28.939
still attached to the booster. The debut of Hot Staging, which fires the upper stage before

00:05:28.939 --> 00:05:35.099
it separates. Observers in post the company has not confirmed noted a stainless steel wool patch

00:05:35.099 --> 00:05:41.299
on one aft flap of Starship 42. A vehicle slated for future flights meant to protect the

00:05:41.299 --> 00:05:45.859
ablative coating under catch points. The heat-resistant layer designed to burn away.

00:05:46.539 --> 00:05:51.559
Worth keeping an eye on, Texas commissioners rejected a public hearing on a 100 percent,

00:05:51.559 --> 00:05:56.999
10-year tax abatement for SpaceX's plan $24 billion star-based data center.

00:05:57.199 --> 00:06:02.159
The proposal had covered turbines and switch gear, and alternative structures that balance

00:06:02.159 --> 00:06:06.819
investment incentives with stable-county income are what remaining local talks would

00:06:06.819 --> 00:06:07.519
have to solve.

00:06:08.396 --> 00:06:13.376
Data center power systems are this episode's engineering deep dive, because silicon and

00:06:13.376 --> 00:06:15.356
turbines do not live on the same clock.

00:06:15.956 --> 00:06:20.516
Computing gear is written off in three to five years, while the gas turbines and grid

00:06:20.516 --> 00:06:26.316
tie-ins around it are built to run 20-30. Take five years of accelerators against a 20-year

00:06:26.316 --> 00:06:32.416
plant, five divided by 20 is one quarter, and each new generation of graphics processing units

00:06:32.416 --> 00:06:38.596
or GPUs replaces the last before the buildings have lived even that quarter. If the tax code

00:06:38.596 --> 00:06:44.216
treats assessed value as steady or climbing, a fast drop in the server's book value still jerks

00:06:44.216 --> 00:06:49.336
the rate around even when output does not change, and as clusters grow, the gap widens.

00:06:49.336 --> 00:06:54.436
Spreading the counties expected take across the project's life avoids letting each year's

00:06:54.436 --> 00:06:55.776
appraisal reset the rate.

00:06:56.256 --> 00:07:01.496
Skip that conversion and the tax-based shrinks every year as servers and GPUs get swapped.

00:07:01.996 --> 00:07:05.076
Forcing rate moves that can exceed 10% year over year.

00:07:05.656 --> 00:07:07.376
It also blocked the opposite swing.

00:07:07.936 --> 00:07:12.496
If values climbed faster than planned, the county's windfall would have been caped while

00:07:12.496 --> 00:07:14.116
the promised amount still arrived.

00:07:14.656 --> 00:07:18.516
Lift that same megawatt into orbit and cooling stops being an air problem.

00:07:18.516 --> 00:07:24.736
Compute above the atmosphere sheds fans and water, then pays in solar array area and radiator

00:07:24.736 --> 00:07:25.156
mass.

00:07:25.796 --> 00:07:30.536
One megawatt from a ground turbine sits on roughly 0.2 square meters of pad.

00:07:31.156 --> 00:07:35.596
Putting that same megawatt on orbit takes tens of square meters of array and radiator.

00:07:36.096 --> 00:07:40.896
On the order of 100 times the ground footprint if you divide those tens by 0.2.

00:07:41.476 --> 00:07:46.676
The trade only closes when the cost to loft a kilogram drops below land, water, and a grid

00:07:46.676 --> 00:07:47.616
hook up on the ground.

00:07:47.616 --> 00:07:51.316
The job Starship's catch and reuse loop is built to do.

00:07:51.796 --> 00:07:56.896
Each successful tower catch of a super heavy booster or a ship lowers the cost of lifting

00:07:56.896 --> 00:08:01.656
the next megawatt of orbital compute, cutting at the extra area that still keeps these

00:08:01.656 --> 00:08:02.516
plants on Earth.

